The shape of `system-stack --format json`<pre><code>{
  "properties": [ { "key": "...", "value": "..." } ],
  "components": [ { "name": "...", "...": "..." } ],
  "gcc": [ { "major": 0, "version": "...", "...": "..." } ]
}
</code></pre> <p><code>components</code> is the list described in Components above.</p> <p><code>properties</code> is a flat list of <code>{"key": str, "value": str}</code> pairs that describe the system itself, not a component. Examples are the OS, the cluster name, and the NVIDIA driver and CUDA versions where a GPU is present.</p> One entry of properties<pre><code>{ "key": "cluster", "value": "daint" }
</code></pre> <p><code>gcc</code> is a list of every installed GCC major version, one entry per version:</p> One entry of gcc<pre><code>{
  "major": 12,
  "version": "12.3.0",
  "prefix": "/usr",
  "c": "/usr/bin/gcc-12",
  "cxx": "/usr/bin/g++-12",
  "fortran": null
}
</code></pre> <p><code>c</code>, <code>cxx</code> and <code>fortran</code> are the path to that language’s compiler driver, or <code>null</code> when the matching package (<code>gcc{N}-c++</code>, <code>gcc{N}-fortran</code>) is not installed. A GCC major version with <code>c: null</code> means the base <code>gcc{N}</code> package itself is missing.</p> <p></p>

The shape of `user-stack --format json`<pre><code>{
  "uenv": { "label": "...", "...": "..." },
  "fabric_providers": [ "..." ],
  "components": [ { "name": "...", "...": "..." } ],
  "envvars": [ { "name": "...", "value": "...", "component": "..." } ]
}
</code></pre> <p><code>components</code> is the list described in Components above.</p> <p><code>uenv</code> identifies the loaded uenv:</p> uenv identity, for prgenv-gnu/25.11:v1<pre><code>{
  "label": "prgenv-gnu/25.11:v1",
  "name": "prgenv-gnu/25.11",
  "mount": "/user-environment",
  "view": "default",
  "arch": "linux-sles15-neoverse_v2",
  "system": "daint"
}
</code></pre> <p><code>fabric_providers</code> is the list of libfabric providers <code>fi_info -l</code> reports, for example the providers compiled into libfabric on a Grace-Hopper node:</p> fabric_providers on a Grace-Hopper node<pre><code>["cxi", "ofi_rxm", "udp", "tcp", "sockets"]
</code></pre> <p><code>envvars</code> is the list of netstack-relevant environment variables that are currently set. Each entry pairs a variable with the component it affects:</p> One entry of envvars<pre><code>{ "name": "FI_MR_CACHE_MONITOR", "value": "kdreg2", "component": "libfabric" }
</code></pre> <p>Without a loaded uenv view, <code>user-stack --format json</code> prints a single error object instead of this envelope:</p> user-stack --format json outside a uenv<pre><code>{ "error": "no uenv view is loaded" }
</code></pre>
